          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bnb",
          "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/followers",
          "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/following{/other_user}",
          "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/gists{/gist_id}",
          "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
          "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/subscriptions",
          "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/orgs",
          "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/repos",
          "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/events{/privacy}",
          "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/bnb/received_events",
          "type": "User",
          "user_view_type": "public",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "created_at": "2026-05-13T18:14:57Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-05-13T18:14:57Z",
        "body": "> This only really comes up at the time of a V8 update, right? Would it make more sense just to add this step to the V8 upgrade checklist, rather than perpetually checking with every commit?\r\n\r\nIf the run time is pretty short (which it seems to be), I don't think it's necessarily bad to run on every commit.\r\n\r\n> I think we are going to have to look at upgrading to temporal_rs 0.2.x before v26.x hits LTS, if the build environment allows (there are [a lot of conformance updates](https://github.com/boa-dev/temporal/releases/tag/v0.2.0) for the stage 4 spec), but we can't update the crates in alignment with the equivalent upstream DEPS update (https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/387bc695b4ab04c008d51f38fc8e531ad9d2d120) because 0.2.0 has been yanked from crates.io, so this script would potentially block such a move.\r\n\r\nDo you think this kind of issue will be repeating or one-off? If one-off, we could just hold off on merging until this is resolved or we could merge with the acceptance that there'll be some wonkiness around that while it gets resolved.",
